  "updated_at": "2023-06-17T19:40:54Z",
  "body": "Sorry, I copy pasted the error after changing the name of the shared library, as a test.\r\n\r\nLooks like it doesn't work without a preceding `./`. Might be a security change in glibc, Fedora 38 uses 2.37.\r\n```\r\n$ LD_PRELOAD=path-mapping.so ls\r\nERROR: ld.so: object 'path-mapping.so' from LD_PRELOAD cannot be preloaded (cannot open shared object file): ignored.\r\nlibpath-mapping.so  LICENSE  Makefile  path-mapping.c  path-mapping.so  README.md  test\r\n$ LD_PRELOAD=./path-mapping.so ls\r\nPATH_MAPPING[0]: /tmp/path-mapping/tests/virtual => /tmp/path-mapping/tests/real\r\nlibpath-mapping.so  LICENSE  Makefile  path-mapping.c  path-mapping.so  README.md  test\r\n```",
  "author_association": "NONE",
  "pin": null,
